## 6. Critical Jupyter Rule

> **Variables stay in memory across cells.**
> If you ran `df = df[['col1', 'col2']]` in a previous cell,
> that damaged `df` stays in memory even if you delete the cell.
>
> **Fix:** Always reload data at the top, or go to **Kernel → Restart & Run All**

