## Common Mistakes to Avoid

```python
# ❌ WRONG — drops columns you might need later
df = df[['col1', 'col2']]
X = df[['col1', 'col2', 'col3']]  # col3 doesn't exist now!

# ✅ RIGHT — select features only when creating X
df['col'].fillna(df['col'].mean(), inplace=True)
X = df[['col1', 'col2', 'col3']]  # all columns still available

# ❌ WRONG — groupby with square brackets
df.groupby['City']['Spent'].mean()

# ✅ RIGHT — groupby with parentheses
df.groupby('City')['Spent'].mean()
```

